## Decision

- **Events are keyed by a bigint** (migration 0004). The 16 hex characters of an event id are 64
  bits; the table keeps them as one number, shifted so that the order of the numbers is the order of
  the hex strings, and every answer still carries the hex string.{% if has("room.freed_mb") %} That frees {{ v("room.freed_mb") }} MB. Rewriting the
  table in place would need a second copy of it, and the plan has no room for one, so the migration
  empties the table and the sync loads it again from the serving release. A load inserts the keys
  in random order and leaves the primary key at {{ v("room.unbuilt_pk_mb") }} MB, so the end of a load rebuilds an index it
  left much larger than a fresh build: {{ v("room.rebuilt_pk_mb") }} MB.{% endif %}

- **The CVE table is vacuumed sooner.** Autovacuum reclaims its dead rows once they pass two percent
  of the table rather than a fifth{% if has("room.bloat_bound_mb") %}, which bounds the room they hold to {{ v("room.bloat_bound_mb") }} MB{% endif %}.
- **Neon holds a scoped corpus.** {% if has("room.corpus_advisories") %}The {{ v("room.corpus_advisories") }} advisories that name a CVE the six stand in products
  carry, the {{ v("room.corpus_kev") }} KEV entries and the {{ v("room.corpus_cwe") }} CWE weaknesses: {{ v("room.corpus_chunks") }} chunks in {{ v("room.corpus_mb") }} MB. {% endif %}The
  short sections of one document share a chunk, so a KEV entry is one chunk and not four; the links
  of an advisory and the notes of a KEV entry are kept with the document and not chunked; and the
  full text index is built on an expression rather than a stored column. The whole corpus, for the
  retrieval and agent evals, lives in Actions, in a Postgres that runs beside the job.
- **The run store is capped.**{% if has("room.run_waiting_cap") %} At most {{ v("room.run_waiting_cap") }} runs wait for a person with every checkpoint; a decided
  run keeps only its latest checkpoint, for at most {{ v("room.run_decided_cap") }} runs, and after that only its record in
  the run tables: {{ v("room.run_store_mb") }} MB at the caps.{% endif %}


